From e1d0a99a55364c08fe1dcc034283c83a7ae1b82e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 23:11:21 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(tui): review of #3908: bounded Stop ack, no sleep in wake
 slots, holder identity

- Stop: skip the take-over when the gateway's durable ledger holds work for the chat
  (a typed prompt already queued there); wait up to 5 s for session.take_over and
  return its error, or, when it fails later, emit an error event the Desktop shows.
- A wake refused by a retiring backend answers "busy" at once (never sleeps inside a
  wake slot); the notice guarantee reads the short retry (15 s) and charges nothing.
- notice_hold_wait: the watcher clears its thread marker in the same locked section
  that decides to return, so a notice refused meanwhile starts a new watcher.
- host_loop_lease: publish and withdraw the retiring record under _RETIRE_MU; withdraw
  it at exit too.
- gateway_background_holder: count a durable holder only in this pid namespace and a
  registry lease only for this host's live process with its recorded start time; the
  gateway must be the very one owner_forward dials for the chat's profile home (its
  endpoint is passed to forward_prompt), else the take-over stays.
- Tests: hold-wait across a lift then an ordinary busy; a forwarded gateway-hosted turn
  waits for the background turn's lease and runs once after; Stop racing a queued
  forwarded admission; failed and late-failing Stops; retire/resume race.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
